course: dictionary
lesson: 8962
title: Simply: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word simply has three main meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Sometimes it means in an easy or plain way: «They lived simply in a small cottage» means they lived without fuss or luxury.
explain: Sometimes simply means only or just. «It is simply a game» means it is just a game, nothing more. Ask yourself: could I put only or just in its place? If yes, that is the meaning.
explain: Sometimes simply means really or completely, to make something stronger. «The fines are simply awful» means they are really awful. Try swapping in really or completely: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Simply is an adverb, a word that tells you more about how, when or how much.
fact: Simply can mean in an easy or plain way, as in «explain it simply».
fact: Simply can mean only or just, as in «it is simply a game».
fact: Simply can mean really or completely, as in «the view was simply beautiful».
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as just, plainly or really, and see if the meaning still fits.
exercise: «Sometimes different ages simply get different things.» What does simply mean here? | Very quickly | Loudly and angrily | Really tired | *Just, only
exercise: «The fines are simply awful.» What does simply mean here? | Only | In a plain, easy way | Slowly and carefully | *Really, completely
exercise: «They lived simply in a small cottage.» What does simply mean here? | *In a plain, easy way, without fuss | Really, completely | Loudly | Only just
test: «It is simply a game, so nobody has to win.» What does simply mean? | Very cold | *Only, just | Plainly and clearly | Really fast
test: «The view was simply beautiful.» Which word could replace simply without changing the meaning? | *Really | Only | Plainly | Slowly
exam: Which sentence uses simply to mean only or just? | «The view was simply beautiful.» | *«It is simply a game.» | «Explain it simply.» | «They lived simply in a small cottage.»
